      "content": "\"Letting exhaustion take over\" means giving yourself permission to stop fighting the inevitable, to stop trying to patch up something that's fundamentally broken. That look on his face is a reflection of his hopes, not a judgment on your worth, and you don't have to carry the weight of his dreams anymore. There is no fixing this, because the only thing that needs fixing is the unbearable pressure you've put on yourself. Just let the tiredness win for a while; it's a quiet way to finally stop the noise.",
